{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 106,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hallelujah! Give thanks to the LORD, for He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who can describe the mighty acts of the LORD or fully proclaim His praise?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed are those who uphold justice, who practice righteousness at all times.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Remember me, O LORD, in Your favor to Your people; visit me with Your salvation,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "that I may see the prosperity of Your chosen ones, and rejoice in the gladness of Your nation, and give glory with Your inheritance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "We have sinned like our fathers; we have done wrong and acted wickedly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our fathers in Egypt did not grasp Your wonders or remember Your abundant kindness; but they rebelled by the sea, there at the Red Sea.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet He saved them for the sake of His name, to make His power known.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He rebuked the Red Sea, and it dried up; He led them through the depths as through a desert.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He saved them from the hand that hated them; He redeemed them from the hand of the enemy.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The waters covered their foes; not one of them remained.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they believed His promises and sang His praise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet they soon forgot His works and failed to wait for His counsel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They craved intensely in the wilderness and tested God in the desert.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So He granted their request, but sent a wasting disease upon them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the camp they envied Moses, as well as Aaron, the holy one of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The earth opened up and swallowed Dathan; it covered the assembly of Abiram.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then fire blazed through their company; flames consumed the wicked.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At Horeb they made a calf and worshiped a molten image.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They exchanged their Glory for the image of a grass-eating ox.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They forgot God their Savior, who did great things in Egypt,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "wondrous works in the land of Ham, and awesome deeds by the Red Sea.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So He said He would destroy them— had not Moses His chosen one stood before Him in the breach to divert His wrath from destroying them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They despised the pleasant land; they did not believe His promise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They grumbled in their tents and did not listen to the voice of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So He raised His hand and swore to cast them down in the wilderness,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "to disperse their offspring among the nations and scatter them throughout the lands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They yoked themselves to Baal of Peor and ate sacrifices offered to lifeless gods.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So they provoked the LORD to anger with their deeds, and a plague broke out among them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But Phinehas stood and intervened, and the plague was restrained.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It was credited to him as righteousness for endless generations to come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At the waters of Meribah they angered the LORD, and trouble came to Moses because of them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they rebelled against His Spirit, and Moses spoke rashly with his lips.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They did not destroy the peoples as the LORD had commanded them,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "but they mingled with the nations and adopted their customs.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They worshiped their idols, which became a snare to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They sacrificed their sons and their daughters to demons.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They shed innocent blood— the blood of their sons and daughters, whom they sacrificed to the idols of Canaan, and the land was polluted with blood.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They defiled themselves by their actions and prostituted themselves by their deeds.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the anger of the LORD burned against His people, and He abhorred His own inheritance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He delivered them into the hand of the nations, and those who hated them ruled over them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their enemies oppressed them and subdued them under their hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Many times He rescued them, but they were bent on rebellion and sank down in their iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless He heard their cry; He took note of their distress.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And He remembered His covenant with them, and relented by the abundance of His loving devotion.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He made them objects of compassion to all who held them captive.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Save us, O LORD our God, and gather us from the nations, that we may give thanks to Your holy name, that we may glory in Your praise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.106.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.106.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Blessed be the LORD, the God of Israel, from everlasting to everlasting. Let all the people say, “Amen!” Hallelujah!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
